From 7871311aa43aaa1f03787839e8a07f3a531f0d1e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Mon, 26 Oct 2026 23:55:08 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/3] VerseRef and text-only chapter shards (U16)

A Scripture reference becomes a door. VerseRef has two modes: link mode
goes to the chapter in the Study Bible; sheet mode is a real link to the
chapter that, on a plain click, opens the verses in the Sheet (U14), read
from a text-only chapter shard, names the Berean Standard Bible with
ScriptureNote, and offers "Open in the Study Bible". A reference the
parser (U09) cannot read stays plain text.

- scripts/build-bible-text.mjs and scripts/lib/bible-text.mjs write
  client/public/bible/text/<book>/<n>.json (verse number and text; John 3
  is 4.5 KB against 42 KB) from bible/ch; --check is the drift gate in CI.
  The shards themselves are the next commit.
- lib/scripture-find.ts finds references in running text and hands each
  to the one parser; RefText and an in-house remark plugin in Markdown.tsx
  (opt-in via verseRefs) make them live; Prose takes verseRefs too.
- ScriptureRef now points at the Study Bible (link mode), not the Passage
  Context tool, and makes each reference in a mixed field live.
- Live references: context guides (body and key texts, sheet), creed
  documents (intro, text, notes, sheet), care plans (sheet), family reading
  plans (sheet), family catechism (link: the verse is printed beside it).
- Tests: shard drift (server), finder, VerseRef, Markdown, ScriptureRef,
  and the pages on real data, including John 3:16 in a context guide.

